PennMUSH pull request #1398 (https://github.com/pennmush/pennmush/pull/1398, not merged upstream):
@http takes a <headers> argument and sets %q<http-overflow>. Applied to the reference PennMUSH by
.github/workflows/parity.yml so that 75-http compares SharpMUSH with what PennMUSH does with it.
SharpMUSH takes the headers as a JSON object rather than #1398's Key:value lines, so 75-http compares
everything but the headers argument.

Taken from the pull request's head (926ab14) against its base (152acc5), less the files `make`
regenerates and the help text, with one fix: the pull request sets http-overflow with
pe_regs_set_int and a string, which stores the pointer as a number; this uses pe_regs_set.

